oard data when checked on 2026-10-18. run_manifest.json records benchmark release osworld-v2-2026.06.24, a Docker provider with a QEMU backend at 1920x1080, a 400-step limit, a screenshot at every step with accessibility tree and OCR on demand, and a multi-attempt policy with one reported result per task. Per task_results.csv, 83 reported results come from initial attempts, 22 from recovery attempts and 3 from retries; the preview table names a different selected attempt for 6 tasks, and the manifest and summary.json give different recovery limits (2 and 3). Each attempt has a card written as instructions to the agent: the solution card opened for task 001 lists the exact schedule entries to enter, the events to delete and the final checks, and the recovery card opened for task 002 plans a guided retry from its parent attempt. summary.json reports a mean score of 0.661 and 43 binary passes over 108 tasks (the preview table marks 44 because task 015 scores 0.9999999999999999); these are publisher measurements from guided, multi-attempt runs and were not reproduced. Linux is established from the Ubuntu Calendar target and /home/user shell commands in task 001. The card declares no license.","published_at":null,"relations":[],"review_status":"curated","scope":"core","summary":"Self-reported OSWorld-V2 run of a Codex-based harness with gpt-5.6-sol on all 108 tasks: per-step CLI and GUI actions, screenshots and scores, plus retried attempts and the solution and recovery cards that guided them.","task_classes":["R11.01.01.02"],"topics":["evaluation","observability"],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/xunsss/osworld2-codex-gpt56sol-0624-multi-attempt"}
